AmpSpread Afterburner Edition v1.0.3-rc1

This plugin monitors 12V-2x6 power cable current balance using per-pin current readings already published by MSI Afterburner's PSU.dll plugin. It is standalone and read-only.

Monitoring features:
- Current spread: highest of six pin currents minus lowest (A).
- Average spread: elapsed-time-weighted mean of reported spread (A).
- Maximum spread: highest spread observed during this monitoring session (A).
- Data complete: 1 when all six pins are present; 0 when unavailable.
- Active port: automatically identifies 12VHPWR port 1 or port 2.

Requirements:
- MSI Afterburner with its PSU.dll plugin enabled and reporting all six pin currents.
- Compatible PSU telemetry exposed through Afterburner hardware monitoring.

Hints:
- The six currents are read from Afterburner's existing monitoring shared memory.
- No separate AmpSpread desktop app, hardware polling, driver or service is required.
- Click Setup to reset the recorded average and maximum between cable tests.
- The plugin retains separate statistics for each PSU port.
- Default graph ranges are 0-1 A (current), 0-0.5 A (average), and 0-1 A (maximum). Afterburner may retain previous custom limits.

Important:
- AmpSpread Afterburner Edition provides measurements only. It does not change PSU settings, trigger safety shutdowns or guarantee protection from connector overheating.
